Experiment: does 0004 remove the refusal on create, because of which the game on 12_0
shows "GPU does not meet the minimum requirements".

The observation that motivates the experiment: with the patched driver the game
creates a device on 12_0 (the 0xc000 refusal is gone), fails to bring the swapchain
up in time and shows a window refusing the requirements, while the log is clean -
not a single err: and not a single Exception. The 0004 refusal returns
VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT from tu_image_init for an image with
SPARSE_RESIDENCY that went to linear (the list of compatible formats
demotes it), and this is exactly the code that the game on 12_0 calls wider than
on 11_1. If after removing the refusal the window disappears and a swapchain appears, the cause is
found; if not - the 0004 refusal is not to blame, and one has to look elsewhere.

The patch touches exactly one check. Removing the gate (exposing
sparseResidencyImage2D in tu_device.cc) stays - otherwise there is nothing to test.
We do not restore the upstream assert: in a release build it is active and would simply
kill the process, which cannot be told from a refusal.

Expected if the hypothesis is right: the game creates the image, the requirements window
disappears, dxgi_vk_swap_chain_init appears in the log.
Expected if the hypothesis is wrong: the window stays, the run behavior does not change.

